"""Source-authored bilingual manuscript. Review scope: depth-review-2026-10-20/REPORT.md."""
from model import p, ref, block, section

PART = dict(title=p('有關打擊洗錢及恐怖分子資金籌集與打擊擴散資金籌集的常識', 'General knowledge on AML/CFT and Counter Proliferation Financing'),
intro=p('理解資金如何被濫用、香港的法律與風險背景，以及制裁和跨境現金申報的作用。', 'Understand how funds are misused, Hong Kong’s legal and risk context, and the roles of sanctions and cross-boundary cash declarations.'), sections=[
section('money-laundering', '洗錢：犯罪得益及三個階段', 'Money laundering: criminal proceeds and three stages', [
    block('定義與過程', 'Definition and process', [
        ('洗錢，簡單來說，就是想辦法讓犯罪得來的財產看起來不像犯罪得益。法律看的是這個意圖：不論財產是全部還是部分、直接還是間接代表犯罪得益，只要行為是為了讓它表面上不像犯罪得益，就可能落入這個定義。另要分開一條不同的罪：處理犯罪得益罪。那是指你在處理財產時，已經知道，或有合理理由相信，它代表犯罪得益。財產不限於現金，表面看起來正經，也不等於沒有問題。例如：把販毒得來的現金拿到兌換店換成外幣，再匯到境外公司帳戶買樓，好讓這些錢看起來像正常生意或投資收入，這就是洗錢的思路。即使櫃檯收到的是「普通現金」，只要你知道或有合理理由相信它代表犯罪得益，處理這筆錢本身也可能構成另一條罪。對應：法定洗錢定義；DTROP／OSCO section 25（處理犯罪得益罪）。', 'Money laundering, in plain terms, is an act intended to make crime proceeds look as if they were not crime proceeds. The legal definition looks at that intention. It covers property that wholly or partly, and directly or indirectly, represents those proceeds. A different offence is dealing with crime proceeds: you deal with property while knowing, or having reasonable grounds to believe, that it represents crime proceeds. Property is not limited to cash, and it need not look suspicious. For example: converting cash from drug sales at an exchange shop, then remitting it through an overseas company account to buy a flat so that it looks like ordinary business or investment income, is the money-laundering idea. Even if the cash looks like ordinary notes, dealing with it may be a separate offence if you know, or have reasonable grounds to believe, it represents crime proceeds. The statutory ML definition is one thing; the DTROP/OSCO section 25 dealing offence is another.'),
        ('洗錢常被分成三個階段來理解。存放（placement），是把犯罪現金放進金融體系，例如分拆存款或兌換。分層（layering），是透過多次轉移、不同帳戶或不同司法管轄區，掩藏資金來源。整合（integration），是讓資金再以投資、資產或業務收益等形式出現，看起來像合法財富。', 'Money laundering is often explained in three stages. Placement introduces criminal cash into the financial system, for example through split deposits or exchange. Layering obscures its origin through transfers, accounts or jurisdictions. Integration returns it as apparently legitimate investments, assets or business income.'),
        ('這三個階段只是幫助理解典型模式的工具。實際一筆交易可以同時涉及多個階段，不必按順序走完。匯款或貨幣兌換業務，可能被用來協助存放及分層。交易看起來有商業外觀，並不表示資金就是合法的。例如：顧客先把大額現金換成外幣（存放），隨即要求分成幾筆匯到不同海外帳戶（分層），這兩步可以發生在同一趟櫃檯交易裡。', 'The three stages are a tool for understanding typical patterns. An actual transaction can overlap more than one stage, and need not follow the stages in order. Remittance and exchange businesses can be used to facilitate placement and layering. A commercial appearance does not establish that the funds are legitimate. For example: a customer first converts a large amount of cash into foreign currency (placement) and immediately asks for it to be split and sent to several overseas accounts (layering). Both steps can happen in a single counter transaction.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第1.9–1.10段', '¶1.9–1.10', 'Placement - the disposal'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('財產及境外犯罪得益的涵義', 'Property and proceeds from overseas conduct', [
        ('在 AMLO 裡，「財產」不限於現金。它也包括貨品、據法權產（choses in action）及土地，不論這些東西在香港還是境外。還包括由該等財產產生的義務、地役權，以及各類產業、權益或收益，無論是現在還是將來、已經既得還是或有的。據法權產是指要用法律行動才能行使的權利。所以，洗錢不能只看有沒有實體鈔票。例如：把犯罪得益轉成一筆銀行存款或一張應收帳款，即使沒有現金過手，那筆可以用法律行動行使的權利本身，仍可以是「財產」。', 'In the AMLO, “property” is not limited to cash. It also includes goods, choses in action and land, whether in Hong Kong or elsewhere, and associated obligations, easements, estates, interests and profits, whether present or future and vested or contingent. Choses in action are rights enforceable by legal action. Laundering is therefore not limited to physical banknotes. For example: turning crime proceeds into a bank deposit balance or a receivable, with no cash changing hands, can still involve “property”, because that right is enforceable by legal action.'),
        ('洗錢定義不只涵蓋在香港可公訴罪行所得的財產。如果某行為在境外發生，但假如在香港做出也會構成可公訴罪行，那些得益同樣可以算進來。「錢是在外國賺的」這一句，並不會自動免除香港的洗錢風險。例如：有人在境外詐騙得來的資金，再到香港金錢服務經營者兌換或匯款。即使原罪行不是在香港發生，只要該行為若在香港做出也會是可公訴罪行，這筆錢在香港仍可能構成洗錢風險。', 'The money-laundering definition covers more than proceeds of Hong Kong indictable offences. It also covers proceeds of overseas conduct that would constitute an indictable offence if it had occurred in Hong Kong. The fact that the money was obtained overseas does not by itself remove Hong Kong laundering risk. For example: funds obtained by fraud overseas are then exchanged or remitted through a Hong Kong money service operator. Even if the original offence did not happen in Hong Kong, the funds may still pose a Hong Kong laundering risk if that conduct would have been an indictable offence here.'),
    ], [
        ref('04', '附表1第1部第1條', 'Schedule 1 Part 1 s.1', 'choses in action'),
        ref('03', '第1.9段', '¶1.9', 'not to appear to be or so represent such proceeds'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('terrorist-financing', '恐怖分子資金籌集：合法資金也可被濫用', 'Terrorist financing: legitimate funds can also be misused', [
    block('與洗錢的分別', 'Distinction from money laundering', [
        ('恐怖分子資金籌集（TF）不只有一種形態。一種是：你提供或籌集財產，而你有意圖或知道，這些財產會全部或部分用於恐怖主義行為；即使後來沒有實際用出去，仍可能構成。另一種是：你向某人提供財產，或提供金融或相關服務；又或者為該人的利益籌集財產或要求服務，而你知道或罔顧該人是否恐怖分子或其聯繫者。這些活動可以直接或間接進行，不能只看資金是從哪裡來的。例如：有人用自己合法賺來的薪水，捐給一個他知道會把錢用於策劃襲擊的組織。即使錢本身來源「乾淨」，仍可能屬於恐怖分子資金籌集。', 'Terrorist financing (TF) is not only one kind of conduct. One form is providing or collecting property intending or knowing that it will be used, wholly or partly, for terrorist acts, whether it is actually used or not. Another is making property, or financial or related services, available to a person, or collecting property or soliciting services for their benefit, knowing or being reckless as to whether they are a terrorist or an associate. Direct and indirect activity is covered. The origin of the funds alone is not enough to decide the issue. For example: a person donates lawfully earned salary to an organisation, knowing it will use the money to plan an attack. Even though the money itself came from a clean source, this may still be terrorist financing.'),
        ('洗錢著重的是財產來自犯罪得益；恐怖活動卻不一定要用「髒錢」。它可以由合法收入、捐款或犯罪收入資助。金額很小、來源看起來合法，或經由註冊組織轉移，都不能自動排除恐怖分子資金籌集風險。例如：一筆小數額、看來像普通善款的轉帳，如果是為已知的恐怖分子或其聯繫者籌集資金，仍可能構成風險。不能因為「錢不多」或「是合法捐款」就當成沒有問題。', 'Money laundering concerns the criminal origin of proceeds. Terrorist activity, by contrast, may be funded by legitimate income, donations or crime. Small amounts, a lawful origin, or a transfer through a registered organisation do not automatically exclude terrorist-financing risk. For example: a small transfer that looks like an ordinary charitable donation may still pose TF risk if it is collected for a known terrorist or associate. “The amount is small” or “it is a lawful donation” does not by itself make the risk go away.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第1.11–1.12、1.23–1.25段', '¶1.11–1.12, 1.23–1.25', 'terrorist financing'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('legal-framework', '香港法律：各條例處理的問題', 'Hong Kong’s laws: the role of each ordinance', [
    block('六組核心法例', 'Six core legal frameworks', [
        ('香港打擊洗錢及相關融資，主要靠六組法例，各管不同事情。先記前三組：AMLO 訂明客戶盡職審查、備存紀錄、監管，以及金錢服務經營者的發牌制度。DTROP 和 OSCO 則處理犯罪得益、披露、調查、限制及沒收。對應：第615章《打擊洗錢及恐怖分子資金籌集條例》（AMLO）；第405章《販毒（追討得益）條例》（DTROP）；第455章《有組織及嚴重罪行條例》（OSCO）。', 'Hong Kong relies on six core legal frameworks, each doing a different job. Start with the first three. Cap.615 AMLO establishes CDD, record-keeping, supervision and MSO licensing. Cap.405 DTROP and Cap.455 OSCO address criminal proceeds, disclosure, investigation, restraint and confiscation.'),
        ('另外三組法例分別處理反恐、聯合國制裁和擴散融資。UNATMO 處理恐怖分子財產、相關服務及披露。UNSO 是在香港實施聯合國安全理事會決議所要求的制裁。第526章則管制可能協助大規模毀滅武器發展、生產、獲取、儲存及運載方式的服務；如果提供服務的人有合理理由相信或懷疑，該服務可能涉及擴散融資，就禁止提供。對應：第575章《聯合國（反恐怖主義措施）條例》（UNATMO）；第537章《聯合國制裁條例》（UNSO）；第526章《大規模毀滅武器（提供服務的管制）條例》。', 'The other three frameworks cover counter-terrorism, UN sanctions and proliferation financing. Cap.575 UNATMO addresses terrorist property, related services and disclosure. Cap.537 UNSO implements sanctions required by UN Security Council resolutions. Cap.526 controls services that will or may assist WMD development, production, acquisition, stockpiling or delivery, and prohibits services where the provider believes or suspects on reasonable grounds that they may be connected to PF.'),
        ('這些條例下的後果不一樣，不要混為一談。DTROP／OSCO 的洗錢罪，最高可罰款港幣500萬元及監禁14年。知悉或懷疑而不披露，最高可罰款港幣5萬元及監禁3個月。通風報訊最高可監禁3年。與恐怖分子資金籌集相關的罪行，可監禁14年及罰款。刑事罪行、披露責任和監管處分，是不同的責任。', 'The consequences under these ordinances are not the same, and should not be mixed up. The DTROP/OSCO laundering offence carries up to HK$5 million and 14 years. Failure to disclose knowledge or suspicion carries up to HK$50,000 and three months. Tipping-off carries up to three years. Relevant terrorist-financing offences carry up to 14 years and a fine. Criminal liability, disclosure duties and regulatory sanctions are distinct responsibilities.'),
        ('OSCO 不只是「多一條洗錢罪」。除其他事項外，它做四件主要的事。第一，賦予香港警方及香港海關人員調查有組織罪行及三合會活動的權力。第二，賦予法院司法管轄權，沒收有組織及嚴重罪行的得益，並可就被告人的財產發出限制令及押記令。第三，增訂一項有關可公訴罪行得益的洗錢罪行。第四，容許法院在適當情況下收取違法者及罪行的資料，以決定是否適宜作出更重的判刑。對應：指引 paragraph 1.20（OSCO 的四項主要作用）。', 'OSCO is not just “one more money-laundering offence”. Among other things, it does four main jobs. First, it gives Police and Customs and Excise officers powers to investigate organized crime and triad activities. Second, it gives the Courts jurisdiction to confiscate proceeds of organized and serious crimes, and to issue restraint and charging orders over a defendant’s property. Third, it creates a money-laundering offence for proceeds of indictable offences. Fourth, it enables the Courts, in appropriate circumstances, to receive information about an offender and an offence to decide whether a greater sentence is appropriate. This is set out in Guideline paragraph 1.20 (OSCO’s four main roles).'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第1.14–1.27、6.1–6.4段', '¶1.14–1.27, 6.1–6.4', 'imprisonment for 14 years'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('六項法例的英文全名及常用縮寫', 'Full names behind the six legal abbreviations', [
        ('前三組法例的英文全名和常用縮寫是：AMLO 是第615章《打擊洗錢及恐怖分子資金籌集條例》；DTROP 是第405章《販毒（追討得益）條例》；OSCO 是第455章《有組織及嚴重罪行條例》。不要把一般可公訴罪行得益的洗錢責任，只限於毒品得益。', 'The English full names and ordinary abbreviations of the first three ordinances are: AMLO: Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorist Financing Ordinance, Cap.615. DTROP: Drug Trafficking (Recovery of Proceeds) Ordinance, Cap.405. OSCO: Organized and Serious Crimes Ordinance, Cap.455. Laundering liability for indictable-crime proceeds is not confined to drug proceeds.'),
        ('另外三組的英文全名是：UNATMO 是第575章《聯合國（反恐怖主義措施）條例》；UNSO 是第537章《聯合國制裁條例》；WMD(CPS)O 是第526章《大規模毀滅武器（提供服務的管制）條例》。三者分別涉及反恐措施、聯合國制裁，以及可能協助大規模毀滅武器的服務，不能混成同一項禁令。', 'The other three English full names are: UNATMO: United Nations (Anti-Terrorism Measures) Ordinance, Cap.575. UNSO: United Nations Sanctions Ordinance, Cap.537. WMD(CPS)O: Weapons of Mass Destruction (Control of Provision of Services) Ordinance, Cap.526. Their counter-terrorism, UN-sanctions and WMD-service controls must not be collapsed into a single prohibition.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第1.14、1.19–1.27段', '¶1.14, 1.19–1.27', 'Drug Trafficking (Recovery of Proceeds)'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('用語邊界：指引中的金融機構', 'Terminology boundary: financial institutions in the Guideline', [
        ('讀指引時，「金融機構」（FI，Financial Institution）這個詞，不一定每次都指同一批香港持牌機構。第03份指引的用語一般沿用 AMLO 的涵義；但詞彙表特別說明，除另有指明外，FI 採用 FATF 建議的定義。只有寫明「AMLO 所界定的金融機構」時，才用該法定範圍。本地電傳、合資格中介人及簡化盡職審查（SDD）各有自己的定義和條件，見第3部分及第6部分。例如：看到「金融機構」時，不要自動當成「所有香港持牌銀行、證券行和金錢服務經營者」的同一份名單。要先看該段是否寫明「AMLO 所界定的金融機構」，還是沿用 FATF 的較廣義用法。', 'When you read the Guideline, the term FI (Financial Institution) does not always mean the same list of Hong Kong licensed institutions. Terms in document 03 generally follow AMLO meanings. Its glossary specifically says FI follows the FATF Recommendations unless otherwise specified, for example “an FI as defined in the AMLO”. Only when the text says “an FI as defined in the AMLO” does the statutory AMLO scope apply. Domestic wires, eligible intermediaries and SDD have their own specified definitions and conditions, which are covered in Parts 3 and 6. For example: do not automatically read every “financial institution” reference as one combined list of Hong Kong licensed banks, securities firms and money service operators. First check whether that passage means an FI as defined in the AMLO, or the wider FATF usage.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第1.2段及「主要用語及縮寫詞彙」金融機構條目', '¶1.2 and Glossary, Financial institution(s)', 'unless specified otherwise'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('international', 'FATF與司法管轄區風險', 'FATF and jurisdiction risk', [
    block('標準、名單與法律須分開理解', 'Distinguish standards, lists and law', [
        ('財務行動特別組織（FATF）是1989年成立的跨政府組織。它制定標準，並推動法律、監管及操作措施的有效實施，以打擊洗錢、恐怖分子資金籌集及擴散資金籌集。香港是成員，必須實施其最新建議。FATF 會透過司法管轄區相互評估及嚴格跟進，監察各地的合規情況，並識別高風險及其他受監察地區。這些建議不是香港法例的替代品。', 'The Financial Action Task Force (FATF) is an inter-governmental body formed in 1989. It sets standards and promotes effective legal, regulatory and operational measures against money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing. Hong Kong is a member and is obliged to implement the latest FATF Recommendations. FATF monitors compliance through jurisdiction evaluations and stringent follow-up, including identifying high-risk and other monitored jurisdictions. Its Recommendations do not replace Hong Kong law.'),
        ('FATF 的風險名單要分兩類來看，而且它們都不是聯合國的指定人士制裁名單。「呼籲採取行動」（call-for-action）這一類，要求加強盡職審查（EDD）；對特定高風險地區，還另有反制措施。「加強監察」（increased monitoring）這一類，須納入風險評估，但並非單單因為被列名，就一律必須做加強盡職審查。例如：某地只被列入「加強監察」，你要把這個因素納入風險評估，但不代表每一個與該地有關的客戶都自動要做 EDD。若某地屬「呼籲採取行動」並指明須採反制措施，要求就更嚴，而且反制措施也不等於只是加強審查。', 'FATF risk lists come in two categories, and neither is a UN list of designated persons. The call-for-action category requires enhanced due diligence, with countermeasures for specified high-risk jurisdictions. Increased monitoring informs risk assessment but does not by itself require EDD in every case. For example: if a place is only on the increased-monitoring list, that factor belongs in your risk assessment, but it does not mean every customer connected with that place automatically needs EDD. If a place is in the call-for-action category and countermeasures are specified, the requirements are stricter, and those countermeasures are not simply another name for enhanced due diligence. FATF risk lists are distinct from UN designated-person sanctions lists.'),
        ('通函上的地區名單是某一天的快照，不是永遠有效的現行名單。2026年7月3日那份通函當時記錄：對朝鮮及伊朗須採取反制措施；對緬甸須採取與風險相稱的加強措施；「加強監察」名單新增波斯尼亞和黑塞哥維那及伊拉克。日常運作必須使用最新的官方更新，不能只記住這一天的名單。對應：document 19（2026年7月3日 FATF 名單通函）。', 'A circular’s country list is a snapshot on a particular date, not a permanently current list. The circular dated 3 July 2026 records countermeasures for the DPRK and Iran, proportionate enhanced measures for Myanmar, and the addition of Bosnia and Herzegovina and Iraq to increased monitoring. Day-to-day operations require the latest official updates, not only this dated list. This is document 19 (the 3 July 2026 FATF-list circular).'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第1.13段', '¶1.13', 'As a member of the FATF'),
        ref('06', '打擊洗錢問答A17', 'AML/CFT FAQ A17', 'conducting EDD is not mandatory'),
        ref('19', '正文第1–3頁', 'Main text pp.1–3', 'Myanmar'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('反制措施不是加強審查的另一個名稱', 'Countermeasures are more than another name for EDD', [
        ('2026年7月3日通函就朝鮮所舉的反制例子，包括終止與其銀行的往來關係、關閉其境內分行或附屬機構，以及限制與朝鮮人士的業務或交易；這些須按適用的機構及法律框架執行。加強審查則包括提高監察的程度及性質。通函也提到緬甸未來可能面對反制，但不要把「將來可能實施」寫成當時已經實施的同一措施。例如：對某客戶提高交易監察的程度，是加強審查的做法；終止與某國銀行的往來關係，則是該通函所舉的反制措施例子，兩者不是同一回事。對應：document 19（2026年7月3日通函第1頁註2、第2頁註5）。', 'The 3 July 2026 circular gives DPRK countermeasure examples including terminating its banks’ correspondent relationships, closing local branches or subsidiaries and limiting DPRK-person business or transactions, within the applicable institutional and legal framework. EDD includes increasing the degree and nature of monitoring. The circular also mentions possible future Myanmar countermeasures; those are not the same as measures already in operation in that snapshot. For example: increasing the degree of transaction monitoring on a customer is an EDD step; terminating correspondent relationships with a country’s banks is a countermeasure example given in the circular. They are not the same thing. See document 19 (3 July 2026 circular, page 1 note 2 and page 2 note 5).'),
    ], [
        ref('19', '第1頁註2、第2頁註5', 'p.1 note 2; p.2 note 5', 'terminating correspondent relationships with DPRK banks'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('sanctions', '恐怖主義及擴散融資的定向金融制裁', 'Targeted financial sanctions for terrorism and proliferation', [
    block('禁止、凍結及許可', 'Prohibitions, freezing and licences', [
        ('定向金融制裁，通常是兩件事一起看：凍結指定人士或實體的資金或其他資產，以及禁止直接或間接向其提供資金、資產或相關服務。篩查不只看國籍或姓名，也須涵蓋有關實體、國家、活動及交易參與者。例如：對方護照不是某個受制裁國家簽發，並不表示可以不做篩查。如果付款最終是為指定實體而做，或交易涉及受限制活動，仍可能落入制裁範圍。', 'Targeted financial sanctions generally do two things: they freeze designated persons’ or entities’ funds or other assets, and they prohibit direct or indirect provision of funds, assets or related services to them. Screening is not only about nationality or names. It also concerns relevant entities, countries, activities and transaction parties. For example: the fact that a counterpart’s passport was not issued by a sanctioned country does not mean screening can be skipped. If a payment is ultimately for a designated entity, or the transaction involves a restricted activity, it may still fall within the sanctions.'),
        ('兩套制裁法例的主管人員不一樣，不要混為一談。在第575章（UNATMO）下，行政長官在憲報刊登有關指定；保安局局長可依權力凍結財產及處理有關許可。在第537章（UNSO）下，實際限制及豁免要看適用規例；法定特許由行政長官批出，申請者須向商務及經濟發展局提出書面申請。例如：涉及 UNATMO 下凍結財產或許可，對口是保安局；涉及 UNSO 下的法定特許，則是向商務及經濟發展局提出書面申請，由行政長官批准。不能把兩個申請窗口當成同一個。', 'The officials who administer the two sanctions frameworks are not the same, and should not be mixed up. Under Cap.575 (UNATMO), the Chief Executive publishes relevant designations in the Gazette, and the Secretary for Security exercises the relevant freezing and licensing powers. Under Cap.537 (UNSO), the actual restrictions and exemptions depend on the applicable regulations. Licences are granted by the Chief Executive, and applicants write to the Commerce and Economic Development Bureau. For example: a freezing or licensing issue under UNATMO is a matter for the Security Bureau; a statutory licence under UNSO is a written application to the Commerce and Economic Development Bureau, for grant by the Chief Executive. These are not the same application window.'),
        ('法定禁止的交易，不是你可以自行選擇接受的「高風險業務」。只有在符合適用法例的豁免，或持有有效許可的情況下，才可以在該範圍內處理。有需要時，還須報告懷疑，並保存處理紀錄。例如：篩查發現對方是指定人士，這不是改為加強審查之後就可以做的生意。除非有適用豁免或有效許可，否則不能向其提供資金或相關服務。', 'A legally prohibited transaction is not simply a high-risk piece of business you can choose to accept. You may deal only within an applicable statutory exemption, or a valid licence where one is available. Where required, you must also report suspicion and keep records of how the matter was handled. For example: if screening shows the counterpart is a designated person, this is not a relationship you can keep by applying enhanced due diligence. Unless an applicable exemption or valid licence exists, you must not make funds or related services available to that person.'),
        ('聯合國作出指定之後，香港本地規例不一定即時跟上，中間可能有時間差。但在本地制裁實施之前，相關活動已經可能觸犯現有的洗錢、恐怖分子資金籌集或擴散融資相關罪行。所以要及早更新風險評估和監察，不能一律等到本地規例生效才行動。例如：聯合國今天把某人列入名單，香港相關規例可能尚未修訂。若在這段空窗期仍與該人進行可能涉及恐怖分子資金籌集的交易，不一定能以「本地名單還沒更新」作為理由，因為現有罪行條文可能已經適用。對應：document 26（說明指定與本地實施之間的時間差）。', 'There may be a gap between a UN designation and its implementation in Hong Kong. Even before local sanctions are implemented, the relevant activity may already breach existing money-laundering, terrorist-financing or proliferation-financing related offences. Update risk assessment and monitoring promptly, rather than automatically waiting for local regulations to come into force. For example: the UN lists a person today, but the relevant Hong Kong regulation may not yet have been updated. Continuing a transaction with that person that may involve terrorist financing during this gap is not necessarily excused by “the local list has not been updated yet”, because existing offence provisions may already apply. This is explained in document 26 (the timing gap between designation and local implementation).'),
        ('擴散融資（PF）要盡快納入機構風險評估，而且要包括現有業務及現有客戶，不只是新客戶。同時要留意指定對象可能利用空殼公司、貿易、代理及複雜付款鏈來規避制裁。對應：document 09（要求把擴散融資納入機構風險評估的通函）。', 'Proliferation financing (PF) should be included promptly in the institutional risk assessment, and that assessment should cover existing business and existing customers, not only new ones. Also consider the risk that designated parties may evade sanctions through shell companies, trade, agents and complex payment chains. This is the call in document 09 (the circular on including PF in institutional assessment).'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第6.1–6.8段', '¶6.1–6.8', 'Secretary for Security'),
        ref('09', '正文第1–2頁', 'Main text pp.1–2', 'proliferation financing'),
        ref('26', '正文第1–3頁', 'Main text pp.1–3', 'time gap'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('全球措施、特定地區與境外制裁', 'Global measures, country-specific measures and foreign sanctions', [
        ('指引會用一些聯合國安理會決議，來說明反擴散措施的兩層結構：全球層面以第1540號及其後決議來說明；針對特定國家的措施，則以朝鮮第1718號、伊朗第2231號及其後決議來說明。但實際禁止及特許，必須按適用的香港法例及更新後的名單判斷。決議的年份本身，不能證明你手上的就是現行名單。', 'The Guideline uses certain UN Security Council resolutions to illustrate a two-tier counter-proliferation structure: a global tier through UNSCR 1540 and its successors, and country-specific measures through DPRK UNSCR 1718 and Iran UNSCR 2231 and their successors. Actual prohibitions and licences still follow applicable Hong Kong laws and updated lists. The year of a resolution does not, by itself, prove that you have a current list.'),
        ('其他司法管轄區自己實施的單邊制裁，一般不會直接變成香港法下的義務。但如果業務是跨境經營，仍可能受境外法規、交易對手要求及業務限制影響，必須理解並管理這方面的風險。', 'Foreign unilateral sanctions generally do not directly impose duties under Hong Kong law. But if you operate across borders, you may still be affected by overseas law, counterpart requirements and business restrictions. That exposure needs to be understood and managed.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第6.9–6.11段', '¶6.9–6.11', 'two-tiered approach'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('安理會第1373號決議與兩套制裁法例', 'Resolution 1373 and the two sanctions frameworks', [
        ('聯合國制裁在香港通常不是「安理會一通過就自動生效」，而要看它是用哪一套法例落實。一般的聯合國制裁，是透過 UNSO（第537章）下的規例在港實施；但涉及恐怖主義的安理會第1373號決議，則由 UNATMO（第575章）處理。行政長官的指明及憲報更新，會使相關指定在港生效。前面所說的時間差風險仍然適用。', 'UN sanctions do not usually take effect in Hong Kong automatically the moment the Security Council adopts them; it depends on which local framework implements them. UN sanctions are generally implemented through regulations under UNSO, Cap.537. Terrorism-related UNSCR 1373 is covered by UNATMO, Cap.575. Chief Executive specifications and Gazette updates give effect to relevant designations locally. The timing-gap risks described above still apply.'),
    ], [
        ref('26', '預期監管標準第1頁', 'Expected regulatory standards, p.1', 'except for UNSC Resolution 1373'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('恐怖分子財產、跨國旅行及間接控制', 'Terrorist property, inter-state travel and indirect control', [
        ('「恐怖分子財產」的範圍，比「犯罪得來的錢」更廣。它包括恐怖分子或其有聯繫者的財產，也包括擬用於或曾用於資助或協助恐怖行為的其他財產。來源合法的財產也可以符合這個定義，不能把恐怖分子財產只理解成犯罪所得。例如：一筆合法薪水或公開募得的捐款，如果是打算用來資助恐怖行為，仍可以是恐怖分子財產。', '“Terrorist property” is wider than “money obtained from crime”. It includes property of a terrorist or an associate, and other property intended or used to finance or assist terrorist acts. Property from a lawful source can still qualify. Do not treat terrorist property as if it were confined to criminal proceeds. For example: lawfully earned salary, or donations raised openly, can still be terrorist property if they are intended to finance a terrorist act.'),
        ('處理恐怖分子財產，以及資助用於恐怖活動的跨國旅行，都有專門禁令。如果你知道或罔顧某財產是否指明恐怖分子財產，或是否指明恐怖分子或其有聯繫者的財產，仍然加以處理，就可能犯法。另外，提供或籌集財產來資助跨國旅行，而你有意圖或知道該旅行是為了實施、計劃、準備、參與恐怖行為或相關訓練，也在禁止之列；不必等到恐怖行為實際發生。例如：即使旅行最後沒有成行，或襲擊沒有發生，只要提供資金時已意圖或知道該跨國旅行是為了準備恐怖行為或相關訓練，仍可能觸及這項旅行資助禁令。對應：UNATMO section 8A（禁止明知或罔顧而處理指明恐怖分子財產等）；section 11L（禁止資助相關跨國旅行）。', 'Dealing with terrorist property, and funding inter-state travel for terrorist purposes, are subject to specific prohibitions. UNATMO section 8A prohibits dealing knowing or reckless as to whether property is specified terrorist property or property of a specified terrorist/associate. Section 11L prohibits providing or collecting property for inter-state travel intending or knowing the terrorist-act, planning, preparation, participation or related-training purpose. An actual terrorist act need not occur. For example: even if the trip never takes place, or no attack occurs, providing funds may still fall within this travel-funding prohibition if, at the time of providing them, you intended or knew that the inter-state travel was for preparing a terrorist act or related training.'),
        ('在 UNATMO 的適用範圍內，保安局局長可以發牌准許例外，例如合理的生活或法律開支，以及法定僱傭款項。金錢服務經營者須向保安局提出申請。這與上文所述、向商務及經濟發展局申請並由行政長官批准的 UNSO 特許，不是同一個窗口。', 'Within UNATMO’s scope, the Secretary for Security can license exceptions, such as reasonable living or legal expenses and statutory employment payments. A money service operator applies to the Security Bureau. This is not the same window as a UNSO licence, which is applied for to the Commerce and Economic Development Bureau and granted by the Chief Executive, as described above.'),
        ('UNSO 適用規例的禁令，不只針對直接被列名的人。它也涵蓋代其行事或按其指示行事的人士或實體、由其擁有或控制的人士或實體，以及由上述人士或實體擁有的實體。除了持有有效法定特許外，禁止直接或間接為其利益提供資金、金融資產或經濟資源，也禁止處理屬於他們、或由其擁有或控制的資產。例如：指定人士不直接出面，而改由他控制的空殼公司收款，這仍可能落入禁令，因為禁令延伸至由其擁有或控制的實體，以及間接為其利益提供資金。', 'The prohibitions in the applicable UNSO regulations are not limited to the person whose name appears on the list. Applicable UNSO prohibitions extend beyond named designees to persons or entities acting for or at their direction, or owned or controlled by them, and to entities owned by the foregoing. Subject to a valid statutory licence, the prohibitions cover making funds, financial assets or economic resources available, directly or indirectly, for their benefit, and dealing with assets belonging to them or owned or controlled by them. For example: if a designated person does not appear in person, but has a shell company he controls receive the payment, this may still fall within the prohibition, because it extends to entities he owns or controls and to indirect provision of funds for his benefit.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第6.5–6.8段及註56', '¶6.5–6.8; footnotes 56', 'section 11L prohibits any person from providing or collecting any property to'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('指引所述的兩層反擴散框架', 'The two-tier counter-proliferation framework in document 03', [
        ('上文所述的兩層反擴散結構，是 document 03 paragraph 6.9 該版原文的結構說明，不是已經核實到今天的完整制裁名單。該對應把全球層面標為安理會第1540(2004)號決議及後續決議，國別層面標為針對朝鮮的第1718(2006)號、針對伊朗的第2231(2015)號及其後續決議。不能把這個框架對應，當成現行完整制裁名單或現行限制。', 'The two-tier counter-proliferation structure described above is the stored edition’s structural mapping in document 03 paragraph 6.9, not a sanctions list verified as complete and current today. That mapping dates the global tier to UNSCR 1540 (2004) and the country-specific tiers to UNSCR 1718 (2006) for the DPRK and UNSCR 2231 (2015) for Iran, and their successors. Do not treat this framework mapping as a verified-current complete sanctions list or set of restrictions.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第6.9段', '¶6.9', 'a two-tiered approach'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('cross-boundary-cash', '跨境現金類物品：超過12萬元的申報制度', 'Cross-boundary CBNIs: declarations above HK$120,000', [
    block('物品、門檻與旅客', 'Items, threshold and travellers', [
        ('跨境要申報的，不只是「大量現鈔」。現金類物品（CBNIs）包括香港或外地的法定貨幣紙幣及硬幣，也包括不記名或其他可透過交付轉移權利的可轉讓票據，例如不記名支票、匯票、旅行支票及本票。要按面值合計，總值超過港幣120,000元，才算「大量」；正好120,000元並沒有超過這個門檻。例如：旅客攜帶正好等值港幣120,000元的現鈔，不算「大量」。若再多一張面值很小的外幣紙幣，合計超過120,000元，就進入申報制度。', 'What must be declared when crossing the boundary is not only “a large amount of cash”. CBNIs include legal-tender notes and coins of Hong Kong or elsewhere, and bearer or other negotiable instruments transferable by delivery, such as bearer cheques, bills, travellers’ cheques and promissory notes. The aggregate nominal value must exceed HK$120,000 to be a large quantity. Exactly HK$120,000 does not exceed the threshold. For example: a traveller carrying cash with a nominal value of exactly HK$120,000 does not have a large quantity. Adding one more low-value foreign note, so that the total exceeds HK$120,000, brings the declaration regime into play.'),
        ('申報方法要看你從哪裡進出。從指明管制站入境，而且管有大量現金類物品的人，須使用紅通道並作書面申報。從其他地方入境的人，以及離境人士，則須應獲授權人員要求作出披露；一旦披露管有大量現金類物品，還須按要求作申報。例如：從指明管制站入境並帶著超過港幣120,000元的現金類物品，應走紅通道並作書面申報，而不是等到關員主動查問才說。若是從其他地方入境或正在離境，則是在獲授權人員要求時披露，披露後再按要求申報。', 'How you declare depends on how you are entering or leaving. At specified entry points, a person who possesses a large quantity of CBNIs must use the red channel and make a written declaration. A person arriving elsewhere, and a person who is departing, must disclose on an authorized officer’s request, and must then declare if a large quantity is disclosed. For example: if you arrive at a specified control point carrying CBNIs worth more than HK$120,000, you should use the red channel and make a written declaration, rather than waiting to be asked. If you arrive somewhere else, or are leaving, you disclose when an authorized officer asks, and then declare as required after that disclosure.'),
        ('「管有」不只指放在口袋或手提行李裡的東西。它包括隨身物品、由該運輸工具運載的個人物品，以及托運行李；托運行李不論是否由、或將會由同一運輸工具運載，都可以計算在內。陪同未滿16歲人士的成人，在知道該幼年人管有大量現金類物品時，須承擔相應責任。如果屬於純粹過境、而且在香港機場未通過入境檢查的法定情況，則獲豁免。例如：把超過門檻的現鈔放在稍後另一班機提取的托運行李裡，並不表示你沒有「管有」這些物品；托運行李仍可計入。若你陪同的孩子帶著大量現金類物品，而你是知道的，相應責任可以落在你身上。', '“Possession” is not limited to what is in a pocket or carry-on bag. It includes personal belongings carried by the person, belongings on the conveyance, and checked baggage. Checked baggage counts whether or not it is carried, or will be carried, on the same conveyance. An accompanying adult has the relevant duties when aware that a person under 16 possesses a large quantity. The statutory airport-transit case, where the person does not go through immigration clearance in Hong Kong, is exempt. For example: placing cash above the threshold in checked baggage to be collected from a later flight does not mean you do not “possess” those items; checked baggage can still count. If a child you are accompanying is carrying a large quantity of CBNIs and you know that, the relevant duty can fall on you.'),
        ('旅客把外幣換成港元來判斷是否超過門檻時，要用有關事件當日的參考匯價。如果當日不是公布日，或事件發生在當天公布之前，則使用前一個公布日的匯價。若不能用這個方法計算，便按法定指定國際機構的匯價；再沒有，才用管有人通常採用的匯價。', 'When a traveller converts foreign currency into Hong Kong dollars to see whether the threshold is exceeded, use the reference rate on the date of the relevant event. If no rate is published that day, or the event happens before publication that day, use the preceding publication day. If the amount still cannot be calculated that way, the statutory fallback is a specified international institution’s rate, and then the rate the holder ordinarily uses.'),
    ], [
        ref('22', '正文第1頁', 'Main text p.1', 'HK$120,000'),
        ref('23', '第2–7條及附表4', 'ss.2–7; Schedule 4', 'nominal value'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('貨物輸入／輸出與違規', 'Cargo imports/exports and breaches', [
        ('如果不是以旅客身分，而是用跨境運輸工具輸入或輸出大量現金類物品，負責人必須事先透過指定電子系統申報。合併計算時，要依 section 10 處理同一運輸工具及同一客戶等情況。系統產生接受申報的參考編號，才視為已經申報。法例並沒有訂出一個統一的「提前24小時」期限，不要自行加上這個時限。', 'For non-traveller imports or exports of large quantities of CBNIs on a cross-boundary conveyance, the responsible person must declare in advance through the designated electronic system. Apply the section 10 aggregation rules, including same-conveyance and same-customer cases. A declaration is made when the system generates the acceptance reference number. There is no invented universal 24-hour deadline in the ordinance, and one should not be added.'),
        ('不是所有貨物都要這樣申報。法定例外包括：適用的旅客物品、只經香港而全程留在飛機或船上的貨物、航空轉運貨物，以及郵包等情況。貨物外幣的匯價基準，通常是上個月15日的參考匯價（若當天不是公布日，則用之前的公布日）。這與旅客以「有關事件當日」為基準不同，不能混用。', 'Not every cargo movement has to be declared in this way. Statutory exclusions include covered travellers’ belongings, goods that remain aboard an aircraft or vessel solely transiting Hong Kong, air-transhipment cargo, and postal packets. Cargo normally uses the previous month’s 15th-day reference rate, or the preceding publication day if that date is not a publication day. That is different from the traveller’s event-date basis, and the two must not be mixed up.'),
        ('沒有遵從申報或披露規定，或作出在要項上虛假的申報或披露，可罰款港幣500,000元及監禁2年。就部分指明罪行，關長可以發出通知，讓人在指定的合理時間內繳付港幣2,000元而不提控。這並不是人人都有的權利：如果已有既往相關定罪或繳付紀錄、有指定的洗錢或恐怖主義定罪，或已按 section 17 檢取物品等情況，便不適用。', 'Failure to comply with a declaration or disclosure duty, or making a materially false declaration or disclosure, can carry a fine of HK$500,000 and imprisonment for two years. For some specified offences, the Commissioner may issue a notice allowing payment of HK$2,000 within a specified reasonable time instead of prosecution. This is not an entitlement for everyone. Relevant prior convictions or payment records, specified money-laundering or terrorism convictions, or seizure under section 17, exclude it.'),
    ], [
        ref('23', '第8–14條、附表5', 'ss.8–14; Schedule 5', 'Written notice about not instituting criminal proceedings on payment'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('現金類物品的五類票據及匯價日期', 'Five instrument forms and the exchange-rate event', [
        ('可轉讓票據這一類，包括以下形式：持有人形式、無限制背書、向虛構受款人付款、所有權隨交付轉移，以及已經簽署但未寫受款人姓名的票據。常見例子有不記名支票、本票、匯票及旅行支票，但必須符合上述票據形式。法定貨幣紙幣及硬幣是另一類。現金類物品並非只有現金和不記名支票才計算。', 'The negotiable-instrument limb includes these forms: bearer form, unrestricted endorsement, a fictitious payee, title passing on delivery, and a signed instrument without a named payee. Common examples include bearer cheques, promissory notes, bills and travellers’ cheques, but only if they meet those instrument-form conditions. Legal-tender notes and coins form the other limb. CBNIs are not limited to cash and bearer cheques.'),
        ('旅客要用哪一天的匯價，取決於「有關事件」是哪一天。就 section 4 來說，有關事件是抵達指明管制站；就 section 5 及 section 6 來說，則是獲授權人員要求披露的那一刻。參考匯價是指香港銀行公會公布的外匯賣出開市參考牌價。套用前面說過的公布日、公布前及後備方法，也不可把這套旅客基準，與貨物上個月15日的基準混用。', 'Which day’s rate a traveller uses depends on what the “relevant event” is. For section 4, the relevant event is arrival at the specified control point. For sections 5 and 6, it is the authorized officer’s disclosure request. Reference rates are the Hong Kong Association of Banks opening indicative counter exchange selling rates. Apply the publication-day, pre-publication and fallback rules described above, and do not mix this traveller basis with the cargo previous-month 15th-day basis.'),
    ], [
        ref('23', '第2(1)、7(6)條', 'ss.2(1), 7(6)', 'signed but does not state a payee’s name'),
        ref('23', '第7條', 's.7', 'means the person arrives at the specified control point concerned'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('檢取與扣留：十個工作日、三個月、兩年', 'Seizure and detention: ten working days, three months, two years', [
        ('檢取現金類物品，與申報制度的「超過港幣120,000元」門檻，不是同一套規則。如果是行使 section 16(1) 的權力時發現現金類物品，而獲授權人員合理懷疑它們屬 OSCO section 25(1) 的犯罪得益，或屬 UNATMO 所指的恐怖分子財產，便可以依 section 17 檢取。這項權力針對的是懷疑財產，不能把申報制度的超過12萬元門檻套進來。例如：關員合理懷疑某旅客手提包裡的8萬元現鈔是犯罪得益，仍可能依這項權力檢取。不能因為還沒超過12萬元申報門檻，就以為一定不可以檢取。', 'Seizing CBNIs is not the same as the declaration regime’s “above HK$120,000” threshold. If CBNIs are found in the exercise of section 16(1) powers, an authorized officer may seize them under section 17 on reasonable suspicion that they represent OSCO section 25(1) crime proceeds, or UNATMO terrorist property. This suspected-property power does not import the declaration regime’s above-HK$120,000 threshold. For example: an officer who reasonably suspects that HK$80,000 in cash in a traveller’s bag represents crime proceeds may still be able to seize it under this power. The fact that the amount is below the HK$120,000 declaration threshold does not by itself mean seizure is impossible.'),
        ('在 section 18 及 section 19 的規限下，section 17 通常准許把檢取的物品扣留至檢取日後不超過10個工作日。這裡的「工作日」不包括星期六、公眾假期、黑色暴雨警告日及烈風警告日，不要直接套用 AMLO 的「營業日」定義。這是物品的扣留期，不是拘捕後扣留人的期限。例如：星期五檢取的物品，其後的星期六、星期日及公眾假期都不算入這10個工作日；也不能改用 AMLO 對營業日的計法來縮短或延長這個期限。', 'Subject to sections 18 and 19, section 17 ordinarily allows the seized property to be detained for no more than ten working days after the day of seizure. “Working days” here exclude Saturdays, general holidays, and black-rainstorm or gale-warning days. Do not substitute the AMLO definition of business days. This is a period for detaining property, not a period of personal custody after arrest. For example: if property is seized on a Friday, the following Saturday, Sunday and any general holiday do not count toward the ten working days. You also cannot use the AMLO business-day method to shorten or lengthen this period.'),
        ('如果懷疑的是犯罪得益，獲授權人員可以在上述期間內，向原訟法庭或區域法院申請 section 18 的繼續扣留令。法院必須信納存在合理懷疑，而且扣留有理據，例如要進一步調查來源，或考慮相關刑事程序、沒收或充公程序。每次命令的期限，不超過自該命令日起3個月。即使再發新命令，總扣留期也不得超過首個法院命令日起計的2年。', 'If the suspicion is of crime proceeds, an authorized officer may, within that period, apply to the Court of First Instance or the District Court for a continuation order under section 18. The court must be satisfied that there is reasonable suspicion and that detention is justified, for example to investigate the source, or to consider relevant criminal, forfeiture or confiscation proceedings. Each order may run for no more than three months from its date. Even if further orders are made, total detention must not go beyond two years from the date of the first court order.'),
        ('兩年並不是全無例外的絕對上限。如果 section 19 所列的相關程序，在扣留期間已經提起，物品可以扣留至該等程序完結。另外，當 section 18 的扣留條件不存在、不再存在，或再沒有理據繼續扣留時，法院可應關係人或有關人員的申請，指示把物品發還。section 18 的延長機制，針對的是懷疑犯罪得益，不應不加區分地當成恐怖分子財產的同一套延長程序。', 'Two years is not an absolute limit with no exceptions. If the relevant proceedings listed in section 19 are instituted during the detention, the property may be detained until those proceedings conclude. Separately, if the section 18 detention conditions do not exist, no longer exist, or detention is no longer justified, the court may, on an application by an interested person or an officer, direct that the property be returned. The section 18 continuation mechanism concerns suspected crime proceeds. Do not indiscriminately treat it as the same extension procedure for terrorist property.'),
    ], [
        ref('23', '第17–19條', 'ss.17–19', 'not more than 10 working days after the day of seizure'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('申報內容的基本清單', 'Basic declaration information', [
        ('申報不能只報一個總額，而要按相應附表填所需資料：旅客用 Schedule 2，非旅客用 Schedule 3。下方參考清單列出這些附表要求的身分、聯絡、運輸工具、現金類物品、日期、來源或目的地，以及擁有人或客戶等資料。', 'A declaration is not complete if it only states a total amount. The required information must be given on the relevant schedule: Schedule 2 for travellers, or Schedule 3 for non-traveller declarations. The reference checklist below sets out the identity, contact, conveyance, CBNI, date, source or destination, and ownership or customer particulars that those schedules require.'),
    ], [
        ref('23', '附表2–3', 'Schedules 2–3', 'If applicable, the name and address of the recipient of the CBNIs'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('貨物的合併與申報責任', 'Cargo aggregation and declaration responsibility', [
        ('貨物要不要合併計算，先分清你是不是承運人，以及「客戶」是誰。非承運人：合併同一人以同一跨境運輸工具輸入或輸出的現金類物品。承運人：合併同一承運人為同一客戶、在同一運輸工具上運送的物品。這裡的客戶必須是直接聘用該承運人的人，或直接聘用代運人、再由該代運人把物品運送或安排運送給承運人的人。如果同一客戶聘用了多名代運人，按這項規則，只有同一代運人運送或安排運送予同一承運人的物品，才合併計算。客戶是指非承運人，不能把物流代運人自行當成客戶。例如：同一客戶請了兩家代運人，分別把現金類物品交給同一承運人、用同一運輸工具運走。按這項規則，不會把兩家代運人的物品全部加在一起；只有同一代運人交給同一承運人的那些，才按此規則合併。', 'Whether cargo CBNIs have to be aggregated depends first on whether you are a carrier, and on who the “customer” is. For a non-carrier, aggregate CBNIs imported or exported by the same person on the same cross-boundary conveyance. For a carrier, aggregate CBNIs carried by the same carrier for the same customer on that conveyance. The customer must directly engage the carrier, or directly engage the forwarder who transports the CBNIs to the carrier, or arranges that transport. If that customer engages more than one forwarder, this rule aggregates only the items transported, or whose transport is arranged, by the same forwarder to the same carrier. “Customer” means a person who is not a carrier. Do not automatically treat the freight forwarder as the customer. For example: the same customer uses two forwarders, each delivering CBNIs to the same carrier for the same conveyance. Under this rule, the two forwarders’ items are not all added together. Only the items of the same forwarder to the same carrier are aggregated under this rule.'),
        ('輸入、輸出，或安排輸入或輸出的人，必須確保事前已經有一份合規申報。如果只是掌管運輸工具，而對該次輸入或輸出沒有其他責任，則有 section 9(2) 的例外。通常以電子方式申報；系統接納並編配參考編號，才算完成。若關長認為電子傳送並非切實可行，則須依關長指示採用另一方式，不是可以自行改用任意紙本程序。旅客、郵包，以及法定過境或航空轉運貨物是否豁除，另按 section 8 判斷。', 'A person who imports or exports, or who causes an import or export, must ensure that a compliant declaration has already been made beforehand. Section 9(2) excepts a conveyance operator who has no other responsibility for that import or export. The declaration is normally made electronically. Submission is complete only when the system accepts it and allocates a reference number. If the CCE considers electronic transmission impracticable, use an alternative manner directed by the CCE, not an arbitrary paper route of your own choosing. Whether travellers, postal packets and the specified transit or air-transhipment cargo are excluded is judged separately under section 8.'),
    ], [
        ref('23', '第8–11條', 'ss.8–11', 'same carrier for the same customer'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('參考：申報資料的完整分類', 'Reference: declaration-information checklist', [
        ('旅客申報要填的資料，可先記這個清單，並按相應表格填報：管有人全名；身分證號碼或旅行證件號碼及簽發地；國籍；出生日期及地點；永久地址（若永久地址在境外，另填在港地址）；運輸工具識別；現金類物品種類及價值；出入境方向、日期及來源或目的地。如果管有人不是物品擁有人，還要填擁有人姓名或名稱及地址；如果是由另一人代報，代報者須另填相同的個人資料。', 'The information required in a traveller declaration can be remembered as this checklist, and must be given on the corresponding form: the possessor’s full name; ID number, or travel-document number and place of issue; nationality; date and place of birth; permanent address (plus a Hong Kong address if the permanent address is overseas); conveyance identifier; CBNI type and value; direction, date, and origin or destination. If the possessor is not the owner, also give the owner’s name and address. If someone else makes the declaration, that declarant supplies the same personal particulars.'),
        ('貨物申報要填的是另一套資料：非承運輸入或輸出人，或承運人客戶的基本資料。如果是自然人，填上述個人資料，但不另列在港地址；如果不是自然人，填名稱、適用的商業登記號碼及業務地址。另外還要填運輸工具、物品種類及價值、方向、日期、來源或目的地，以及在適用時填收受人姓名或名稱及地址，以及貨單等批次識別資料。', 'A cargo declaration uses a different set of particulars: basic information of the non-carrier importer or exporter, or of the carrier’s customer. Individuals provide the personal particulars mentioned above, but without a separate Hong Kong-address item. Entities provide the name, the applicable business-registration number and the business address. Also give the conveyance, type and value, direction, date, and origin or destination and, where applicable, the recipient’s name and address and a consignment identifier, such as a waybill number.'),
    ], [
        ref('23', '附表2、3', 'Schedules 2–3', 'Information to be Provided in Declaration'),
    ], kind='reference'),
]),
])
